1999/01/15 "with" level interferes with "for" variable check.

The fact that "with" nests the level was confusing the check for local
variable in "parfor". Added "wthlvl" variable, this keeps track of the
"with" nesting level. Since "with" is the only level change within a
code block, that is subtracted from the "level" variable before check.

1999/01/16 "with" level interferes with "goto" target check.

As above, gotos that cross out of a "with" statement were erroneously
tagged as external block references. Used with level to correct.
